{"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&ref=sha256%3Af31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5%2Fevidence%2Fmapping.long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","record":{"command":[],"details":"The papers' evidence mapping names these Lean declarations for Long record Proposition 1.2 (realising finite monotone witness rules). Long record prop:257-finite-witness-rule: lean.status exact_or_stronger. Relation note: The Lean statement takes any upward-closed predicate $U$ on finite sets of naturals with $U(E)$ and not $U(\\varnothing)$; the printed family $\\mathcal U$ on subsets of $E$ is the case $U(S)\\iff S\\cap E\\in\\mathcal U$, which is upward closed because intersection with $E$ preserves inclusion, and then $U(\\mathcal P\\cap E)$ reads $\\mathcal P\\cap E\\in\\mathcal U$. The host $H$ omits $0$, so it is a set of positive integers; `Summable (Set.indicator H primeWeightedTerm)` is $W_{b,\\mathcal P}(H)<\\infty$ for nonnegative terms, and failure of summability of $1/a$ on $H$ is the printed divergence. Sources: evidence/paper_evidence.json at 3368d1e69467. Scope: copied from the papers' evidence mapping; this example did not review the correspondence.","id":"mapping.long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","kind":"semantic_review","source_ids":["evidence_mapping"],"status":"not_run","subject_ids":["lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.finite_monotone_witness_rule_realised","long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule"],"tool":"Copied from the papers' evidence mapping (plectis-paper-evidence/2); no review by this example"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/evidence/mapping.long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-257-finite-witness-rule","id":"field:03e84c5e58eece3c847be3728c7601c